Happy to help — this is general, public industry-standard knowledge (the FHIR spec is published by HL7), so no patient data involved.

Here's a typical FHIR **Patient** resource with the most common fields:

```typescript
interface FhirPatient {
  resourceType: "Patient";
  id: string;
  meta?: {
    versionId?: string;
    lastUpdated?: string;
    profile?: string[];
  };
  identifier?: Array<{
    system?: string;
    value?: string;
    use?: "usual" | "official" | "temp" | "secondary" | "old";
  }>;
  active?: boolean;
  name?: Array<{
    use?: string;
    family?: string;
    given?: string[];
    prefix?: string[];
    suffix?: string[];
  }>;
  telecom?: Array<{
    system?: "phone" | "fax" | "email" | "pager" | "url" | "sms" | "other";
    value?: string;
    use?: string;
  }>;
  gender?: "male" | "female" | "other" | "unknown";
  birthDate?: string; // ISO 8601: "YYYY-MM-DD"
  deceasedBoolean?: boolean;
  deceasedDateTime?: string;
  address?: Array<{
    use?: string;
    line?: string[];
    city?: string;
    district?: string;
    state?: string;
    postalCode?: string;
    country?: string;
  }>;
  maritalStatus?: {
    coding?: Array<{ system?: string; code?: string; display?: string }>;
  };
  contact?: Array<{
    relationship?: Array<{ coding?: Array<{ system?: string; code?: string }> }>;
    name?: { family?: string; given?: string[] };
    telecom?: Array<{ system?: string; value?: string }>;
  }>;
  communication?: Array<{
    language: { coding?: Array<{ system?: string; code?: string; display?: string }> };
    preferred?: boolean;
  }>;
  managingOrganization?: {
    reference?: string;
    display?: string;
  };
}
```

The key field names you mentioned and a few notes:

- **`resourceType`** — always `"Patient"` for this resource.
- **`id`** — the logical ID (not the MRN; MRNs usually live in `identifier` with a specific system URI).
- **`identifier`** — array of identifiers (MRN, SSN, drivers license, etc.), each with `system` and `value`.
- **`name`** — array of `HumanName`, where `family` + `given[]` are the important parts.
- **`birthDate`** — a string, not a `Date` object, formatted `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- **`gender`** — constrained to the four values above (FHIR R4).

The canonical reference is the HL7 FHIR spec: **`http://hl7.org/fhir/patient.html`** (R4) — worth bookmarking for your interfaces, since FHIR R5 has a few differences (e.g., more granular `genderIdentity`, `sex`, and `recordedSexOrGender` fields).

Just to be clear on the boundary: this is public spec knowledge, so it's fine to share. What I can't do is tell you Scioto Ridge Health's own internal patient schema or field mappings — that'd be internal data and outside my scope. For your dev work, mock data against the public FHIR spec is the right approach.
